// Regression test: an explicit `to`-cast involving a generic type
// parameter used to be rejected UNCONDITIONALLY at the TEMPLATE's own
// definition site, regardless of whether any real instantiation would
// have made the cast legal -- src/TypeCheckerExpr.cpp's `visitCast()` cast-
// legality whitelist had no bypass for `TurfGenericParamType`, unlike
// every other type-checking path in this compiler (equality, argument
// matching), which all defer the real check to a per-instantiation
// clone's own re-typecheck. Found live while investigating whether
// `mem::Pool<T>` could gain a genuine generic `free_all()` method
// (docs/development/changes/STD-003.md) -- a cast from a generic
// parameter failed to compile even where the only real caller
// instantiates a type the cast is already legal for.
import test;

// The minimal repro: a cast from a plain generic PARAMETER (not a field
// access -- see this test's own final note below for why that distinction
// matters) to a concrete type, inside a generic function -- used to fail
// at THIS declaration regardless of whether castToInt() is ever called.
fn<T> castToInt(x: T): int {
  return x to int;
}

fn main(): int {
  test::assert(castToInt(42) == 42, "cast from a genuinely-int-instantiated T works");

  // A DIFFERENT instantiation, to prove the fix isn't int-specific -- int32
  // is the only OTHER primitive type this same cast (`to int`) is legal
  // for, per the existing whitelist (`int32 -> int`).
  immutable thirtyTwo: int32 = 7 to int32;
  test::assert(castToInt(thirtyTwo) == 7, "cast from a genuinely-int32-instantiated T works too");

  return 0;
}

// NOTE (kept for a future session, not a live regression): the identical
// cast, written as `self.v to int` inside a generic METHOD reading its own
// struct's `v: T` FIELD (as opposed to a plain parameter, above), still
// fails -- `self.v`'s type resolves through GlobalSymbolTable's own
// registered TurfStructType for the struct, whose fields are permanently
// stuck as NamedType("T") rather than TurfGenericParamType("T") (a
// separate, deeper gap; see TypeCheckerCall.cpp's own "NamedType, not
// TurfGenericParamType" doc comment on visitMethodCall's Subst recovery
// for the mechanism this shares). This fix's own dynamic_cast only
// recognizes TurfGenericParamType, so it does not reach that case. Not
// pursued as part of STD-003 -- lower value (mem::Pool<T> is the only
// place it would matter, and it is always instantiated at a pointer type
// in practice) and higher risk (touching field-type resolution is a
// larger, less-contained change than this fix).
